A||||5||Ronnie||Getrag 5spd question?||||6||
Z||000000||Ronnie||01-29-2001||10:22 PM||||Could someone please clarify this for me? What Fieros came with the Getrag 5 spd? Also, what's the difference in it and the 5spd Muncie? Plus, wasn't there a 5spd Isuzu also? I know some of you Guru's know this.<BR>How do you identify the differences?<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd / Silver '87GT 5spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BOTHGTS_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Hank is Here||01-29-2001||10:30 PM||||Getgag and Muncie are the same tranny, different names same animal.   All 6cyl 5 speed are Getrag.  All 4 banger 5 spd trannies are Isuzu's.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||01-29-2001||11:04 PM||||All '84 Fieros had Muncie built 4 speeds.  (either 4.10 or 3.32 ratio).  The 4.10 has the RPO code of M19 and the 3.32 is MY8.<P>All '85-'88 4-cyl. Fieros had Isuzu built 5-speeds. (3.35 ratio).  Can't remember the RPO code.<P>All '85 and most '86 V-6 Fieros had Muncie built 4 speeds (3.61 ratio).  These are commonly referred to as Muncies.  RPO code M17.<P>Some '86 and all '87-'88 V-6 Fieros had Getrag designed, Muncie built 5-speeds (3.65 ratio).  These are commonly referred to as Getrags.  RPO code MG2.<P>So basically all 4-speeds (whether 4-cyl. or V-6) were built by Muncie, all 4-cyl 5-speeds were Isuzu built and all V-6 5-speeds were Getrags.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 01-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||01-29-2001||11:11 PM||||Thanks guys! That was what I wanted to know.A friend and I were really getting confused on all this since the Fiero Finders book didn't refer to them as Getrag.And they also mention a Saginaw trans.<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd / Silver '87GT 5spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BOTHGTS_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||ray b||01-29-2001||11:15 PM|||| gertag v6 only stock 5spd<BR> muncie v6 only stock 4spd<P> isuzu 4cly only stock 5spd<BR>  muncie 4cly 4spd two diff rear end ratio 4.10 and 3.xx correct?<BR>                ray<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 01-29-2001).]||||reg||1
